{"content":"I have enough to answer comprehensively.\n\nq20. **Mechanism:** Server-Sent Events (SSE) — a long-lived HTTP stream where each connected client is a subscriber holding a buffered event channel; the server pushes JSON-encoded events over it (not WebSocket).\n\n**Hub path:** `server/router/api/v1/sse_hub.go` — the `SSEHub` struct (line 56) with `NewSSEHub` (63), `Subscribe`/`Unsubscribe` (71/89), `Close` (99), and `Broadcast` (115), which fans out an `SSEEvent` to all clients whose visibility/role checks (`canReceive`, line 134) pass.\n\n**Handlers that broadcast through `s.SSEHub.Broadcast(...)`:**\n- `CreateMemo` — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:163` (sends `SSEEventMemoCreated`, skipped when called internally from `CreateMemoComment`)\n- `DeleteMemo` — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:585` (`SSEEventMemoDeleted`)\n- `CreateMemoComment` — `server/router/api/v1/memo_service_comments.go:126` (`SSEEventMemoCommentCreated`)\n- `UpsertMemoReaction` — `server/router/api/v1/reaction_service.go:106` (`SSEEventReactionUpserted`)\n- `DeleteMemoReaction` — `server/router/api/v1/reaction_service.go:161` (`SSEEventReactionDeleted`)\n- `dispatchMemoUpdatedSideEffects` (helper) — `server/router/api/v1/memo_update_helpers.go:71` (`SSEEventMemoUpdated`), which is itself called from `UpdateMemo` (`memo_service.go:513`), `SetMemoAttachments` (`memo_attachment_service.go:48`), and `SetMemoRelations` (`memo_relation_service.go:48`) — so these three RPCs broadcast indirectly through that shared helper.","iteration":9,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
